Twos attached to letters, labels, or subscripts get larger values than ordinary
numerical twos. Completing 30/31 is positive, especially in calendar dates.
Roman and typographic twos, code-indentation NBSPs, and NUL separators also
contribute. Separate boundary rules handle initial digits, a Title: header,
code declarations/comments and carriage-return runs. Unmatched text is zero;
word-specific variation is deliberately omitted. State resets per document.
